The contest consists of the following categories: Oral Interpretation (O'I and O'H);
Dramatic Interpretation;
Dramatic Performance (includes Improvisation); and
Individual or Group Performance (includes Dance, Speech, etc.), which may include the categories of
Individual or
Group Improvisation;
Dance;
Percussive; 
Other (such as storytelling or music, etc.).

The contest covers a number of elements that have been changed this year. These changes follow.

SPEECH (O'I and O'H):
The category of Individual Interpretation for both O'I and O'H requires students to perform from written texts. However, for some contests up to the state level and for some grades, the requirement may include the option of the original student-made or adapted text (written, edited). This would depend on the division or level they are competing at (division I or division II, etc). This applies also to the Dramatic Interpretation.

